From 1ffc465b8ddae9231a11fbb31544b38bde3ed0c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jakub Zelenka <jakub.zelenka@openssl.foundation>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 19:50:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] x509: fix leak of issuer alt names on reserve failure in
 copy_issuer()
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When copying the issuer subject alt names into the subject issuer alt
name extension, a failure to reserve space in the destination stack
freed only the decoded stack and leaked all the names it still owned.

Free the names together with the stack on the error path.

Found by the fuzz mfail CI job on the x509v3 corpus.

Fixes: aa066b9e6e44 "Add more functionality to issuer alt name and subject alt name. New options to include email addresses from DN and copy details from issuer certificate. Include examples in openssl.cnf, update Win32 ordinals."
Complements: fa856b0ce0f5 "Fix memory leak on failure in copy_issuer()"
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5-1
Reviewed-by: Saša Nedvědický <sashan@openssl.org>
Reviewed-by: Eugene Syromiatnikov <esyr@openssl.org>
Merge-date: Wed Nov  4 22:37:55 2026
Merged-from: https://github.com/openssl/openssl/pull/33542
(cherry picked from commit 5922e34b192cef0837a5e7ac8200afd9b97b7624)
---
 crypto/x509/v3_san.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/crypto/x509/v3_san.c b/crypto/x509/v3_san.c
index 0defca0..b5e7aa3 100644
--- a/crypto/x509/v3_san.c
+++ b/crypto/x509/v3_san.c
@@ -380,7 +380,7 @@ static int copy_issuer(X509V3_CTX *ctx, GENERAL_NAMES *gens)
     return 1;
 
 err:
-    sk_GENERAL_NAME_free(ialt);
+    sk_GENERAL_NAME_pop_free(ialt, GENERAL_NAME_free);
     return 0;
 }
 
